# STATUS: draft — needs vendor-baseline + BSP source analysis

## Goal
Port Ethernet (stmmac DWMAC) controller support from Amlogic GKI 6.6 BSP into mainline. S905X5M/S7D has 1× GbE RGMII interface (likely RTL8211F-CG PHY). Identify glue layer differences vs SM1 variant.

## BSP source to diff against
```
DannieDarko/odroid-c5_linux_common_drivers (to be cloned)
├── drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-meson8b.c (S7D variant?)
├── drivers/net/phy/realtek.c                           (RTL8211F support)
├── arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/s7d_meson_eth.dtsi
└── arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/s7d_s905x5m_odroidc5.dts (eth node + pinctrl)
```

## Mainline file(s) to extend
```
torvalds/linux (v6.16+)
├── drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-meson8b.c (S7D variant logic)
├── drivers/net/phy/realtek.c                           (already supports RTL8211F)
├── arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/amlogic-s7d.dtsi       (eth node stub)
└── arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/amlogic-s7d-s905x5m-bm202.dts (no eth — add!)
```

## Expected diff outline
- compatible string: `"amlogic,s7d-dwmac"` (DT binding update in Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/amlogic,dwmac.yaml)
- Glue layer: register offsets, clock gating, reset sequencing vs SM1
- RGMII timing: delay tuning (check hw errata vs SM1 — calibration register shifts?)
- PHY config: RTL8211F negotiation (1000base-T full duplex, RGMII mode bits)
- DTS: eth node w/ clocks/resets/phy-handle, pinctrl groups for RGMII pads

## Open questions
- [ ] Does S7D DWMAC glue use identical register layout as SM1 (dwmac-meson8b)?
- [ ] RGMII delay tuning: which registers, same bit shifts as SM1?
- [ ] PHY detection: does RTL8211F auto-negotiate or need firmware patch?
- [ ] Clock: eth_core_clk vs sm1_eth_clk — same CLKID?
- [ ] Reset: does eth need PLL_ETH reset, same as SM1?
- [ ] PCB pinout: RGMII pin group mapping — same group name as C4, or new?
- [ ] Interrupt: PHY IRQ line from GPIO, same as C4?

## Upstream submission target
- netdev@vger.kernel.org
- Cc: Francescon Meda, Giuseppe Cavallaro, linux-amlogic@lists.infradead.org
- Get_maintainer.pl on patch (TBD)
- Binding doc MUST accompany

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] BSP ETH driver diffed vs mainline (identify hw glue deltas)
- [ ] Minimal patch authored (compatible + binding + pinctrl DTS node)
- [ ] Kernel builds clean (CONFIG_STMMAC_ETH=y, CONFIG_REALTEK_PHY=y)
- [ ] DTS boot w/ eth node, dmesg shows link detection
- [ ] `ip link show eth0`, ping test from host → success
- [ ] DT binding YAML updated + yamllint passes
- [ ] Posted to netdev + Signed-off-by
